Z||000000||Haze_Performance||10-24-2000||04:24 AM||||Well its been 10 days since I got my 87 SE from fierodave. First I put on some new rubber. Also upgraded sub in a stock sub box. I pulled out <B>all</B> the interior to clean & repair. (you can do almost anything with a torx bit and a 7mm socket  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol)Installed all the drivers side ground FX.(I still need some parts to install the pass. side)  Put on some 84 (glass) sail panels. Put it a new column & steering wheel. Minor wing stud repair. Its not road ready yet, but its getting there. <P>Please check out my post in the Mall. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001593.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/001593.html</A> <P><BR>Ill post some pic's soon of the car when I was at fierodaves putting it on the car dolly & what it looks like now.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif"> <BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A>-                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||10-24-2000||10:44 AM||||Haze, since it sounds like you've got most of the interior out.  Have you thought about taking out the seats and power wash the carpets at a coin wash.  I did mine, and it was well worth the little extra work.  Keep us posted on the progress.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
